  "question": {
    "text": "Two vectors <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>X</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">Y</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">&#8594;</mo></mover></math> have equal magnitude. The magnitude of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">X</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">&#8594;</mo></mover><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">-</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">Y</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> times the magnitude of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">X</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>Y</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></math>. The angle between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>X</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">Y</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">&#8594;</mo></mover></math> is :",
